**30 cm** deep.", "How much space does the tank take up? How much water is in it? Are these the same thing? Think about it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Litres and millilitres", "p": ["1 litre = 1000 mL."], "qq": {"id": "m6u11s2t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "2.5 L in mL?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2500, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "2500."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Volume", "p": ["**Volume** is the amount of **space a 3D shape takes up**, measured in cubes: cm³, m³.", "Cuboid: **volume = length × width × height**. Tank: 50 × 30 × 40 = **60 000 cm³**."], "fig": {"kind": "solid", "solid": "cuboid", "a": "50 cm", "b": "30 cm", "c": "40 cm"}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Capacity", "p": ["**Capacity** is **how much a container can hold** (usually liquid), measured in mL and L.", "Link: **1 cm³ = 1 mL**, so 1000 cm³ = 1 L. The tank's capacity is 60 000 cm³ = **60 L**.", "Water 30 cm deep: 50 × 30 × 30 = 45 000 cm³ = **45 L** – that's the volume of water, not the capacity of the tank."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Volume", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m6u11s2t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Volume of a cuboid 6 cm × 4 cm × 5 cm (cm³)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 120, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "120."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I work with volume and capacity?", "p": ["Step 1: Volume of a cuboid = l × w × h (in cubes).", "Step 2: Capacity = how much it holds (mL, L).", "Step 3: 1 cm³ = 1 mL; 1000 cm³ = 1 L.", "Step 4: Read questions carefully: full container or part-filled?"]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Counting cubes", "p": [], "q": "A cuboid of cubes: 5 long, 3 wide, 2 high.", "steps": [["5 × 3 = 15 per layer", ""], ["2 layers → 30", ""]], "a": "30 cubes"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Capacity in litres", "p": [], "q": "A box 20 cm × 10 cm × 10 cm. Capacity?", "steps": [["2000 cm³", ""], ["2 L", ""